        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 1090,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:03:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1075,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 1091,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152102,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 1091,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fallopian tube</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:03:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1076,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 1092,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152103,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 1092,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most women with these tumours are asymptomatic, and the majority of cases are an incidental finding at the time of surgery for another gynaecological disorder. Adenofibromas are mainly located in the fimbria {9421082}. Papillomas may cause tubal obstruction or occur without symptoms {3176920; 3721698} and are loosely attached to the tubal mucosa in the lumen.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:03:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1077,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 1093,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152104,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 1093,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are rare entities occurring in women of reproductive age (24&ndash;45&nbsp;years) {39877487}. The reported frequency of fallopian tube adenofibromas in salpingectomies ranges from about 2% to 30% {31972564; 18580316; 26630221; 24820399; 28319576}. Tubal papillomas are exceedingly rare tumours primarily described in case reports {39877487}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:03:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1078,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 1094,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152105,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 1094,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There are conflicting data as to whether these lesions are more or less common in individuals with <em>BRCA1/2</em> mutations or a strong family history of breast/ovarian carcinoma than in women who are not at high risk {26630221; 18580316}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:03:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1079,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1095,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152106,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 1095,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The pathogenesis for tubal adenofibromas and papillomas is unknown. A<em> BRAF </em>(c.1799T&gt;A) mutation (Val600Glu) has been identified in one papilloma case {29851866}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:03:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1086,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1102,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152107,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 1102,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most adenofibromas are &lt;&nbsp;10&nbsp;mm and many are microscopic; uncommon features include multicentricity and bilaterality {18580316}. Papillomas usually appear as an intraluminal friable tissue &lt;&nbsp;30&nbsp;mm in diameter {24442176}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:03:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1080,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1096,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152108,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 1096,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Adenofibromas have admixed epithelial and mesenchymal components and may be cystic. The dense fibromatous stromal component can be nodular or have papillary growth. Tubal-type epithelium (mixture of secretory and ciliated cells) covers the surface of the papillae or lines cystic spaces. Papillomas are composed of delicate, branching fibrovascular stalks lined by bland cuboidal to columnar epithelial cells. These two tumours can show overlapping morphological features that may result in interobserver variation in separating the entities. However, the distinction is of no clinical significance.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:03:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1081,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1097,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152109,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 1097,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:03:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1082,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 1098,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152110,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 1098,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:03:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1085,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 1101,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152111,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 1101,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<p>Adenofibroma: benign, biphasic tumour composed of bland tubal-type epithelium and fibromatous stroma.</p>\r\n<p>Papilloma: benign, delicate papillary proliferation attached to the tubal mucosa.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:03:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1083,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 1099,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152112,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 1099,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:03:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1084,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 1100,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152113,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 96,
        "headingId": 1100,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Both adenofibroma and papilloma have a benign clinical course.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:03:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
